#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0e0e0e"))
  #line-at(105.3pt, 82.28pt, "Partial Collapse and Ensemble Invariance under Continuous Quantum Measurement ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(224.85pt, 107.53pt, "Shalender Singh*")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(307.88pt, 107.53pt, ", ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(313.38pt, 107.53pt, "Santosh Kumar ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.6pt, 120.05pt, "PolariQon Inc., Palo Alto, California, USA")
  #line-at(267.35pt, 132.8pt, "(December 2025)")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(285.63pt, 158.05pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 184.8pt, "Wavefunction collapse is often regarded as an unavoidable consequence of quantum measurement. Here ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 197.33pt, "we show that in driven–dissipative quantum systems, continuous measurement can extract information ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 210.08pt, "without disturbing the physical steady-state ensemble. Using the stochastic master equation formalism, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 222.83pt, "we identify measurement-invariant steady states whose unconditional density matrix remains unchanged ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 235.33pt, "under continuous monitoring, despite the presence of measurement-induced collapse at the level of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 248.08pt, "individual quantum trajectories. This separation between conditional collapse and ensemble invariance ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 260.58pt, "leads to a regime of partial collapse, in which measurement-induced localization is transient and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 273.32pt, "continuously counteracted by dissipation and drive. We establish a necessary and sufficient condition for ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 286.1pt, "steady-state invariance under continuous measurement and show that it holds over a finite range of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 298.6pt, "measurement strengths. Our results clarify how information gain and measurement backaction can be ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 311.35pt, "dynamically decoupled in open quantum systems, with implications for continuous quantum sensing and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 324.1pt, "the foundations of nonprojective measurement. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 350.6pt, "I. INTRODUCTION ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 377.37pt, "Quantum measurement is traditionally associated with unavoidable disturbance of the measured system, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 389.87pt, "culminating in wavefunction collapse [1–3]. In closed systems, this intuition is formalized by projective ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 402.62pt, "measurement theory, where information gain and state disturbance are fundamentally inseparable [4]. In ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 415.12pt, "contrast, many contemporary quantum platforms operate far from equilibrium, sustained by continuous ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 427.87pt, "drive and dissipation and naturally described by open quantum system dynamics [5–7]. In such settings, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 440.4pt, "the relationship between measurement, information, and disturbance is more subtle and remains an active ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 453.15pt, "subject of investigation. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 479.9pt, "Continuous quantum measurement provides a particularly sharp lens on this distinction [8–11]. When a ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 492.4pt, "system is monitored weakly and continuously, the evolution of the quantum state depends on whether one ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 505.15pt, "conditions on the measurement record. At the level of individual trajectories, continuous measurement ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 517.67pt, "induces stochastic localization—often interpreted as gradual collapse—while the ensemble-averaged state ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 530.42pt, "evolves deterministically under a modified master equation [12–15]. This separation between conditional ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 543.17pt, "and unconditional dynamics raises a fundamental question: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(335.15pt, 543.17pt, "must continuous measurement necessarily ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 555.92pt, "disturb the physical steady state of an open quantum system?")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 582.42pt, "In this work, we show that the answer is no. We identify a broad class of driven–dissipative quantum ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 594.95pt, "systems that admit ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(156.58pt, 594.95pt, "measurement-invariant steady states")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(329.15pt, 594.95pt, ", for which the unconditional density matrix ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 607.7pt, "remains unchanged under continuous monitoring. In these systems, measurement extracts genuine ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 620.45pt, "information and induces collapse at the level of conditioned trajectories, yet the physical steady-state ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 632.95pt, "ensemble is preserved. This separation gives rise to a regime of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(353.9pt, 632.95pt, "partial collapse")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(425.93pt, 632.95pt, ", in which measurement-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 645.7pt, "induced localization is transient and continuously counteracted by the system’s native dissipative ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 658.45pt, "dynamics. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 684.97pt, "Our results rely only on standard open quantum system theory and do not invoke modifications of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 697.725pt, "quantum mechanics. Instead, they clarify how measurement backaction can be dynamically neutralized at ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 710.225pt, "the ensemble level, even when the measurement is informationally nontrivial. We derive a necessary and ")
]

