  #line-at(72.025pt, 136.05pt, "3.2 Interpretation and Scope")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 162.55pt, "Equation (8) provides a necessary and sufficient condition for non-invasive continuous probing at the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 175.55pt, "ensemble level. Importantly, this condition does not require the measurement operator ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(454.2pt, 175.55pt, "𝑐")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(459.7pt, 175.55pt, " to commute with ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 188.3pt, "the full system Hamiltonian, nor does it imply the absence of measurement backaction at the level of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 200.83pt, "conditioned trajectories. Rather, it states that the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(287.63pt, 200.83pt, "unconditional")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(348.4pt, 200.83pt, " effect of measurement—pure dephasing ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 213.83pt, "generated by ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(131.3pt, 213.83pt, "𝒟[𝑐]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(152.83pt, 213.83pt, "—acts trivially on the steady ensemble. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 240.58pt, "Measurement-invariant steady states therefore generalize familiar notions such as quantum non-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 253.08pt, "demolition measurements and decoherence-free subspaces, while remaining distinct from both. In ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 265.83pt, "particular, the measurement may extract nontrivial information and induce stochastic localization in ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 278.35pt, "individual trajectories, even as the physical ensemble remains unchanged. The resulting dynamics ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 291.1pt, "naturally lead to the notion of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(205.33pt, 291.1pt, "partial collapse")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(277.38pt, 291.1pt, ", which we analyze in the next section. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 317.85pt, "3.3 Minimal illustrative example: thermalized qubit with QND monitoring")
