  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0e0e0e"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 191.05pt, "This simple example illustrates how continuous measurement can induce strong, stochastic localization in ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 203.58pt, "individual trajectories while dissipation restores the steady ensemble, a mechanism that underlies the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 216.33pt, "partial collapse and dissipative uncollapse phenomena discussed in the next section. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 249.83pt, "4. PARTIAL COLLAPSE AND DISSIPATIVE UNCOLLAPSE")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 276.35pt, "We now characterize the dynamical consequences of measurement-invariant steady states at the level of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 288.85pt, "conditioned evolution. Although continuous measurement leaves the unconditional steady state ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 301.6pt, "unchanged, it nonetheless induces stochastic localization of the conditioned state. This localization ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 314.35pt, "constitutes a form of ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(165.58pt, 314.35pt, "partial collapse")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(237.6pt, 314.35pt, ", whose defining feature is its transient and reversible character. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 340.85pt, "Within the stochastic master equation (3), partial collapse arises from the innovation term proportional to ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 353.87pt, "ℋ[𝑐]")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.8pt, 353.87pt, ", which continuously updates the conditioned state based on the measurement record. For a ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 366.37pt, "measurement-invariant steady state satisfying Eq. (8), this localization does not alter the ensemble-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 379.37pt, "averaged density matrix, but instead produces fluctuations of the conditioned state around ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(470.2pt, 379.37pt, "𝜌")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(475.95pt, 381.62pt, "ss")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(484.2pt, 379.37pt, ". The ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 392.12pt, "conditioned dynamics may therefore be viewed as a sequence of temporary excursions away from the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 404.87pt, "steady ensemble, followed by relaxation driven by the underlying dissipative processes. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 431.37pt, "This competition between measurement-induced localization and dissipative restoration defines a natural ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 444.4pt, "timescale hierarchy. Measurement tends to localize the conditioned state over a timescale set by ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(497.2pt, 443.9pt, "(𝜂Γ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(512.72pt, 446.65pt, "𝑚")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(520.98pt, 444.4pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(525.48pt, 440.4pt, "−1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(536.22pt, 444.4pt, ", ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 457.4pt, "while dissipation restores the steady ensemble over a characteristic relaxation time associated with ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(508.7pt, 457.4pt, "ℒ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(515.48pt, 457.4pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 469.9pt, "When these timescales are comparable, the system exhibits intermittent localization and delocalization, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 482.65pt, "with no net disturbance to the steady state. In this regime, collapse is neither instantaneous nor permanent, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 495.4pt, "but instead appears as a dynamical, continuously reversed process. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 521.92pt, "We refer to this restoration mechanism as ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(258.35pt, 521.92pt, "dissipative uncollapse")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(360.15pt, 521.92pt, ". Unlike protocols that reverse ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 534.67pt, "measurement backaction through active feedback or postselection, dissipative uncollapse arises ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 547.17pt, "autonomously from the system’s native dynamics. Importantly, uncollapse here is not defined as a ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 559.92pt, "deterministic reversal of a specific measurement outcome, but rather as the physical recovery of the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 572.67pt, "steady ensemble under continued evolution. Averaging over measurement records yields ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(246.85pt, 599.2pt, "lim ")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(246.85pt, 605.95pt, "𝑡→∞")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(266.35pt, 599.2pt, "𝔼[𝜌")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(283.13pt, 601.45pt, "𝑐")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(287.88pt, 599.2pt, "(𝑡)] = 𝜌")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(325.63pt, 601.45pt, "ss")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(334.15pt, 599.2pt, ",")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(368.15pt, 599.2pt, "(16) ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 630.2pt, "independent of the prior measurement history. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 656.7pt, "This perspective clarifies the role of collapse in continuously monitored open systems. Measurement-")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 669.47pt, "induced collapse is not eliminated, but confined to the level of conditioned trajectories, where it manifests ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 682.23pt, "as transient localization. At the ensemble level, collapse is rendered dynamically reversible by dissipation, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 694.725pt, "allowing information to be extracted without steady-state disturbance. This separation between ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 707.475pt, "conditional collapse and unconditional invariance provides a physically grounded notion of non-invasive ")
]

// arXiv source page 6
#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 82.28pt, "continuous measurement and highlights the fundamentally non-projective character of measurement in ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 95.03pt, "non-equilibrium quantum steady states. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#0e0e0e"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 121.55pt, "Notably, measurement-invariant steady states are fully compatible with quantum Zeno localization at the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 134.05pt, "trajectory level: in the strong-measurement regime individual trajectories may be pinned near eigenstates ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 146.8pt, "of the monitored observable, while dissipation induces rare transitions whose stationary mixture ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 159.55pt, "preserves the ensemble-averaged steady state. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 192.8pt, "5. IMPLICATIONS AND OUTLOOK ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.025pt, 219.33pt, "The existence of measurement-invariant steady states clarifies how information gain and measurement ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 232.08pt, "backaction can be dynamically decoupled in open quantum systems. In driven–dissipative settings, ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 244.83pt, "continuous measurement need not disturb the physical ensemble, even though it induces collapse at the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 257.33pt, "level of conditioned trajectories. This separation sharpens the distinction between collapse as a physical ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 270.08pt, "process and collapse as conditioned knowledge, and highlights the fundamentally non-projective nature of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 282.85pt, "measurement in non-equilibrium quantum steady states. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 309.35pt, "From a practical perspective, measurement-invariant steady states provide a principled framework for ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 322.1pt, "non-invasive continuous probing. Because the steady ensemble remains unchanged, long-time monitoring ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 334.6pt, "can be performed without compromising stability, making such states naturally suited to continuous ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 347.35pt, "quantum sensing, parameter estimation, and persistent monitoring protocols. More generally, they offer a ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 359.87pt, "route to accessing dynamical information encoded in measurement records without degrading the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 372.62pt, "underlying state. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 399.37pt, "At a foundational level, our results show that collapse is not an unavoidable consequence of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 411.87pt, "measurement, but a dynamical feature whose physical impact depends on the interplay between ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 424.62pt, "measurement, drive, and dissipation. In particular, ensemble invariance demonstrates that information ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 437.15pt, "extraction and state disturbance need not coincide, even in the absence of feedback or postselection. This ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 449.9pt, "perspective complements and extends existing treatments of continuous measurement and quantum ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 462.65pt, "trajectories by identifying a regime in which collapse is transient and dynamically reversible. ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 489.15pt, "Looking forward, measurement-invariant steady states suggest natural connections to resource-theoretic ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 501.9pt, "approaches to quantum measurement and nonlocality, where physically accessible information—rather ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 514.42pt, "than projective outcomes—defines operational resources. They also motivate further exploration of ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 527.17pt, "continuous measurement in strongly driven and non-equilibrium systems, where steady-state structure and ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 539.67pt, "measurement backaction can be engineered independently. More broadly, these results emphasize that the ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 552.42pt, "foundations of quantum measurement are most transparently revealed not in isolated systems, but in open ")
  #line-at(72.025pt, 565.17pt, "systems sustained far from equilibrium.")
]

